0 Gear Train
0 Name: gear-train.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // A 1x8 Technic brick holding three gears on 2L axles: 8 tooth, 24 tooth, 40 tooth.
0 // Turning the 8 tooth gear once turns the 40 tooth gear 1/5 of a turn, the same way.
0 // Holes are 10 LDU below the brick's top; gears sit in front of the brick, at z = -20.

0 // Step 1: the brick
1 14 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3702.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: 2L axles through holes 1, 3 and 7, sticking out in front
1 0 -60 10 -10 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3704.dat
1 0 -20 10 -10 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3704.dat
1 0 60 10 -10 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3704.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: gears, 40 LDU (8 + 24 teeth) and 80 LDU (24 + 40 teeth) apart.
0 // The 24 tooth gear is turned half a tooth (7.5 degrees) so its teeth fall between its neighbours'.
1 72 -60 10 -20 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3647.dat
1 71 -20 10 -20 0.991445 -0.130526 0 0.130526 0.991445 0 0 0 1 3648.dat
1 71 60 10 -20 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3649.dat
0 STEP
